			"ChannelTitle": "Kanishk Nishar",
			"Description": "Friday, November 4, 2011\r\nSaturday, November 5, 2011\r\nSunday, November 6, 2011\r\n\r\nBrahms Third \r\nJoAnn Falletta, conductor\r\nMichael Ludwig, violin\r\n\r\nBPO Concertmaster Michael Ludwig is featured as soloist in Wieniawski\u0027s Violin Concerto No. 2, one of the greatest violin concertos of the Romantic era, memorable for its lush and moving melodies and harmonies. JoAnn Falletta conducts the program, which also includes Wieniawski\u0027s countryman, Mieczys\u0142aw Kar\u0142owicz\u0027s Symphonic Poem \u0022A Sad Tale\u0022 and Brahms\u0027 Third Symphony. Built around the tonal theme of F-A flat-F, the symphony celebrates \u0022Free But Happy\u0022 (Frei aber froh) and is one of the composer\u0027s most popular.",
